==Dutch==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|lesschen}}, from a merger of two {{inh|nl|odt}} verbs:
* {{m|odt|*leskan}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*leskaną}}; class 5 strong, intransitive.
* {{m|odt|*lesken}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*laskijaną}}; class 1 weak, causative of the first verb.

The former verb is cognate with Old High German {{m|goh|leskan}} (German {{m|de|löschen}}).

The latter verb is cognate with Old Saxon {{m|osx|aleskian}}, Old High German {{m|goh|lesken}} (German {{m|de|löschen}}).

====Verb====
{{nl-verb|leste|gelest}}

# to [[quench]] (thirst)

=====Conjugation=====
{{nl-conj-wk|les|lesse}}

